\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces The BC$\to $RL pipeline. (a)~The PointNet encoder and actor MLP are trained end-to-end on expert demonstrations with MSE loss. (b)~The encoder is frozen and the actor MLP is fine-tuned with PPO alongside a state-based asymmetric critic. (c)~At inference the critic is discarded; the encoder and actor run deterministically.}}{7}{figure.caption.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:bcrl_pipeline}{{4}{7}{The BC$\to $RL pipeline. (a)~The PointNet encoder and actor MLP are trained end-to-end on expert demonstrations with MSE loss. (b)~The encoder is frozen and the actor MLP is fine-tuned with PPO alongside a state-based asymmetric critic. (c)~At inference the critic is discarded; the encoder and actor run deterministically}{figure.caption.5}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces The grasp-and-remove crane environment. Each parallel environment contains a log loader crane positioned above a rack with 200 cylindrical logs spawned in randomized configurations. At each step, the policy selects a grasp target and a fixed FSM controller executes the pick sequence.}}{7}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:environment}{{5}{7}{The grasp-and-remove crane environment. Each parallel environment contains a log loader crane positioned above a rack with 200 cylindrical logs spawned in randomized configurations. At each step, the policy selects a grasp target and a fixed FSM controller executes the pick sequence}{figure.caption.6}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {II}{\ignorespaces Evaluation results across 100 episodes with randomized 200-log pile configurations (mean $\pm $ std). The heuristic uses privileged pose state. RL variants use a symmetric actor-critic (shared encoder provides auxiliary gradient); BC variants use a PointNet encoder with identical architecture; BC$\to $RL uses an asymmetric actor-critic (frozen BC encoder for actor, state-based MLP critic). RL fails regardless of observation type; for BC, raw PC matches or exceeds segmented PC across all metrics.}}{7}{table.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:results}{{II}{7}{Evaluation results across 100 episodes with randomized 200-log pile configurations (mean $\pm $ std). The heuristic uses privileged pose state. RL variants use a symmetric actor-critic (shared encoder provides auxiliary gradient); BC variants use a PointNet encoder with identical architecture; BC$\to $RL uses an asymmetric actor-critic (frozen BC encoder for actor, state-based MLP critic). RL fails regardless of observation type; for BC, raw PC matches or exceeds segmented PC across all metrics}{table.caption.8}{}}
